  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nLow level clouds are breaking up from the southwest as low level \nflow veers southerly and favorable theta-e advection develops. This \nreturn flow of moisture will provide an axis of lower 70 dewpoints\nand moderate instability. An outflow boundary tracking across \neast Indiana will be the focus for convective development this \nafternoon. Effective shear is limited to around 20 kts so do not \nexpect great organization to storms. DCAPE values around 1000 J/KG \npoint to the potential for strong to isolated damaging winds. \nMachine learning guidance continues to be focused on the Tri-State \nregion for strong to damaging winds. PWAT values approach 2 inches,\nso heavy rain could produce heavy rain, but storms should be \nprogressive enough to keep any flooding localized. Will continue to \nmessage these threats with the timing between 3 pm over our west to 7\npm across the southeast.",
